{"id": "unknown-2026-11-08-004", "date": "2026-11-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Avaco posts its third straight quarterly loss, but expects a strong Q4 as OLED equipment shipments begin", "content": "<p>Korea-based OLED equipment maker <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/avaco\">Avaco</a> reported its financial results for Q3 2026, with revenues of 47.3 billion won (about $34.8 million USD), down 6% from Q3 2025, and an operating loss of $3.4 million USD. This is Avaco's third straight quarterly loss - but the company expects a large profit swing in Q4 2026, as it started shipping major OLED equipment to its customers at the end of October.</p><p><img class=\"align-center\" src=\"https://www.oled", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/avaco-posts-its-third-straight-quarterly-loss-expects-strong-q4-oled-equipment", "type": "rss"}]}
